## Before You Start: Revoke Compromised Secrets

**Your `.env` files contain real API keys that are in git history.** Do this first:

1. Go to https://resend.com/api-keys → Revoke the exposed key
2. Generate new secrets in your terminal:
   ```bash
   # JWT secret (64+ characters)
   openssl rand -base64 48

   # Database password (alphanumeric only - special chars can break URLs)
   openssl rand -base64 24 | tr -dc 'a-zA-Z0-9'
   ```
3. Create a new Resend API key at resend.com
4. **Save these somewhere secure** (password manager, not a text file)

